          "verdict": "malicious",
          "analysis": "The sample is an ARM-based Linux malware, likely an IoT worm or bot. It exhibits multiple malicious behaviors: it performs network scanning by sending SSDP discovery probes (`M-SEARCH` to `255.255.255.255:1900`) to find other devices (`sub_ae5c`). It conducts extensive reconnaissance by enumerating processes and network connections via the `/proc` filesystem (`sub_e844`, `sub_dee4`). It searches for downloader utilities like `wget`, `curl`, and `tftp` in an attempt to fetch additional payloads (`sub_e844`), and terminates other processes using `kill` signals (`sub_c838`, `sub_e844`). The malware also uses a fake User-Agent (`Google Chrome/60.0.3112.90 Windows`) to disguise its network activity.",
